Thanks @coilysiren!

@dearchap, I should have made the distinction clearer. A flag.Value alone isn't enough. The value in that example also implements flag.Getter, so the cli.Value assertion succeeds. The panic happens later in FlagBase.Set.

Here's the same case with a custom type, without the standard flag package or a runtime type assertion:

```go
package main

import (
	"context"

	cli "github.com/urfave/cli/v3"
)

type textValue struct{ text string }

func (v *textValue) String() string
